  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The mirror",
  "description": "Use cones to set out two squares of about 5 × 5 metres that share one side (not to scale). Players work in pairs and one pair is active at a time. They stand in separate squares, facing each other. A leads and moves quickly between the cones in their square. B follows like a mirror image in the other square.\n\nChange pairs after about 10 seconds. Next time the pair is up, they swap roles.\n\nProgression: start without stick or ball, then with stick only, and finally with stick and ball.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep your eyes up so you see both the ball and your partner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Small, quick steps and a low centre of gravity make it easier to change direction."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Leader: vary the speed and direction to challenge the mirror."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ask the players: which movement was easiest to follow, and which was hardest?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 1,
